WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.250
A useful handover gives the recipient the right artifact
and enough context to use it.

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:16.795
A portable document supports continued editing; plain
Plant UML source supports text based reuse; images and PDF
support reading and presentation.

00:00:16.915 --> 00:00:25.915
We will preview and download the supported image formats,
inspect encoded renderer links, and create local
presentation views and review notes.

00:00:26.035 --> 00:00:29.535
Finish by checking the files you intend to deliver.

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:36.492
Open File, Export and Preview export.

00:00:36.612 --> 00:00:41.437
Select SVG and inspect the full drawing, margin and
background.

00:00:41.557 --> 00:00:46.132
SVG is useful when a recipient needs a scalable diagram.

00:00:46.252 --> 00:00:52.627
The export includes the rendered image rather than editor
selections and interaction overlays.

00:00:52.747 --> 00:00:57.847
Check long labels, clipping and authored appearance in the
preview before downloading.

00:00:57.967 --> 00:01:05.317
Keep the file alongside the document so the recipient can
distinguish the readable picture from the editable
project.

00:01:08.833 --> 00:01:13.983
Choose PNG for a raster image that can be inserted into
many documents.

00:01:14.103 --> 00:01:18.303
Raster scale changes pixel dimensions and memory use.

00:01:18.423 --> 00:01:26.048
Increase it only as far as the intended output requires,
then inspect readability and the estimated image size.

00:01:26.168 --> 00:01:29.218
Choose a suitable margin and background.

00:01:29.338 --> 00:01:37.613
If the app reports an image size limit, reduce scale or
use SVG rather than repeatedly attempting an oversized
export.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:44.983
Select PDF and review its page and image bounds.

00:01:45.103 --> 00:01:52.328
This PDF output uses a white page with a rasterized
diagram, so it is different from a vector SVG.

00:01:52.448 --> 00:01:56.373
Check the result at the reading size the recipient will
use.

00:01:56.493 --> 00:02:02.693
A very wide schedule may be better shared as a scalable
image or the portable document as well.

00:02:02.813 --> 00:02:09.738
Download the PDF after checking the preview, and include a
clear title and revision context in the handover.

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:17.667
File Export also provides plain source and clipboard
formats.

00:02:17.787 --> 00:02:26.362
Plain source is useful for text workflows, but it does not
replace a connected portable document with retained
application information.

00:02:26.482 --> 00:02:34.957
Copy as Markdown and Copy for Confluence prepare content
for their destination; review what was copied before
pasting it into a shared page.

00:02:35.077 --> 00:02:38.702
Copying and preparing content do not publish it.

00:02:38.822 --> 00:02:45.297
Keep private or unfinished work in your practice
environment until the intended handover is ready.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:53.725
Export Source to obtain the plain Plant UML text for the
active diagram.

00:02:53.845 --> 00:02:57.395
Download it and compare it with the authored statements.

00:02:57.515 --> 00:03:07.815
The source is useful for text workflows and other
compatible renderers, but it does not carry the complete
application document, connected members or retained
history.

00:03:07.935 --> 00:03:14.085
Keep the portable project as well when the recipient needs
to continue the full application workflow.

00:03:14.205 --> 00:03:18.055
Check which diagram member is active before exporting.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:25.867
Copy as Markdown prepares a fenced Plant UML code block.

00:03:25.987 --> 00:03:30.862
After copying, inspect the actual clipboard content in
this training preview.

00:03:30.982 --> 00:03:39.382
Copy for Confluence prepares the corresponding wiki macro
markup; inspect that content too before pasting it into
the destination.

00:03:39.502 --> 00:03:44.552
These commands prepare text, and do not publish a page or
send a message.

00:03:44.672 --> 00:03:51.472
Keep source disclosure and destination permissions in mind
when moving a real project into another system.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:00.100
Copy image prepares a rendered picture for a destination
that accepts images.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:07.570
Choose the command from File and Export, then inspect the
actual PNG read from the clipboard in this training
preview.

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:12.415
Check the dimensions and that all task labels and the
milestone are visible.

00:04:12.535 --> 00:04:19.735
A copied image is a snapshot; it does not carry the
editable document, history or connected diagram members.

00:04:19.855 --> 00:04:26.180
Keep the portable source alongside a shared picture when
the recipient needs to continue editing.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:35.500
Link and embed creates an encoded source URL, not a
collaboration invitation.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:41.020
Encoding is not encryption: someone with the URL can
recover the source.

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:49.540
Opening or embedding that URL sends the source to the
chosen renderer, and external rendering can differ from
this app's local preview.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:54.160
Review the renderer address and disclosure before
generating a link.

00:04:54.280 --> 00:05:00.130
Generating the text locally does not mean the eventual
image is an offline artifact.

00:05:03.633 --> 00:05:07.258
Open Presentation and local review from View.

00:05:07.378 --> 00:05:13.078
Presentation gives the diagram a read only stage with
navigation and review tools.

00:05:13.198 --> 00:05:18.373
Use Fit and zoom for the audience rather than changing
task dates to fit a screen.

00:05:18.493 --> 00:05:23.443
Open the local review panel to choose diagram objects and
add highlight steps.

00:05:23.563 --> 00:05:31.763
A focused explanation should guide the audience through a
few meaningful objects, not animate every item simply
because it is available.

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:40.567
Open presentation from a connected document rather than a
separate diagram.

00:05:40.687 --> 00:05:46.537
Use its diagram selector to move between the work
breakdown structure and the linked schedule.

00:05:46.657 --> 00:05:52.057
Fit the selected diagram for the audience and confirm
which member is being presented.

00:05:52.177 --> 00:05:59.552
Presentation navigation changes the view, while the
connected document retains the authored member sources and
links.

00:05:59.672 --> 00:06:03.172
Return to the editor when you need to change the plan.

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:10.975
Use a view name to save a meaningful sequence of highlight
steps.

00:06:11.095 --> 00:06:15.945
Choose an object, write a personal review note and anchor
it to that object.

00:06:16.065 --> 00:06:19.690
These views and notes are stored locally in the browser.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:24.835
They are not included in the portable file, exports or
live collaboration.

00:06:24.955 --> 00:06:28.405
Another person will not receive them automatically.

00:06:28.525 --> 00:06:36.100
Include the required explanation explicitly in your
handover, and revisit an anchor if the underlying diagram
changes.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:45.175
Rendered links are working controls, so review their
destinations before opening them.

00:06:45.295 --> 00:06:49.645
Activate the Portal reference and check the browser
confirmation.

00:06:49.765 --> 00:06:55.340
Cancel this first request and verify that the diagram and
source remain unchanged.

00:06:55.460 --> 00:07:01.410
Accept the second request to open the reference in a
separate tab without replacing the editor.

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:08.980
The exported SVG also retains the link destination; check
the actual artifact when preparing a handover.

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:18.300
Web links and mail links use the confirmation guard, while
cross diagram member connections and collaboration
invitations remain separate features.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:27.725
Finish with a portable project, the required plain source
and readable exported diagrams.

00:07:27.845 --> 00:07:34.445
Reopen the project and inspect connected members, labels,
schedule assumptions and retained history.

00:07:34.565 --> 00:07:38.940
Open the images and PDF at their intended reading size.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:45.710
Include the project start date, status date and important
assumptions so a reader can interpret the plan.

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:50.880
Document limitations honestly; Jira is excluded from this
edition.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:55.025
A good handover makes the next person's first action
clear.
